<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<h2>Decode requests</h2>
<p><code>DecodeJSON</code> wraps <code>json.NewDecoder(req.Body).Decode</code> for the common case. Unknown fields are an error.</p>
<pre><code>type CreateUser struct {
    Name string `json:"name"`
}

var input CreateUser
if err := router.DecodeJSON(req, &amp;input); err != nil {
    _ = router.BadRequest(w, err)
    return
}</code></pre>

<h2>Write responses</h2>
<p><code>JSON</code> sets <code>Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8</code>, writes the status code, and encodes the value.</p>
<pre><code>_ = router.JSON(w, http.StatusCreated, input)</code></pre>

<h2>Error helpers</h2>
<ul>
    <li><code>Error</code></li>
    <li><code>BadRequest</code></li>
    <li><code>InternalServerError</code></li>
    <li><code>MessageError</code></li>
</ul>
<p><code>Error</code> writes <code>{"error": "..."}</code> with the error's message, or the status text when the error is <code>nil</code>. <code>BadRequest</code> and <code>InternalServerError</code> are <code>Error</code> with their status, and <code>MessageError</code> makes an error from a message.</p>
</article>

